			<div class="content" id="post-content-2329108">
									

<p>Special thanks to Hornby, Wogglebug, GhostActual, and Michael Atreus. You guys are great.</p>
<p>Hornby, who is the author of <a href="/scp-1050">SCP-1050</a>, gave me permission to reference his article (no longer part of the article), helped me in a major way, and oversaw many of the revisions.</p>
<p>I drew inspiration from <a href="/scp-1050">SCP-1050</a>, <a href="/scp-163">SCP-163</a>, and other articles.</p>
<div style="text-align: center;">
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">PLEASE READ THE FOLLOWING BEFORE VOTING OR COMMENTING:</span></strong></p>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">&quot;I know it is cliche, but only if you actually believe what -1 &quot;tells&quot; you. It could have no idea what it is talking about. It could be confused. It could be desperate for attention after who-knows-how-long alone and cannot maintain its composure for long until it ends up sulking and moping (I particularly like this one). It could be lying. The Foundation might be misinterpreting the patterns completely; perhaps -1 is not sentient at all, and the patterns on 2929 are simply random (although extremely improbable) products of a probabilistic universe. The reader and the Foundation simply do not know.&quot;</span><br />
<span style="text-decoration: line-through;"><em>-ooblex, 2015</em></span></p>
</blockquote>
</div>
<hr />
<p>e: Changes to the log are in progress, but will not be complete for anywhere from a couple to 10 days due to reasons outside of my control.</p>
<p>ee: Finished! Please disregard any of my comments that no longer apply due to the edit.</p>
<p>eee: Thanks Decibelles for fixing a spelling error!</p>

